{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows low positivity (0.00) and true prices show persistent downward drift.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent high prices when sentiment includes a positive signal (e.g., 0.33 or 0.50) to avoid underestimating upward momentum.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction if forecast is significantly above true price for 3+ consecutive days, especially after a spike.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes by applying a 1-2 day lag correction, particularly when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "When sentiment history includes a 0.67 signal, increase forecast volatility to reflect market overreaction, but cap at 5% above recent high.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, apply a downward bias correction if true price consistently underperforms forecast by >10% over 5+ days, especially with low sentiment."
  ]
}
